.TH RR2GRAPH 1 "May 2026" "rr2graph 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rr2graph \- process and visualize blood pressure, pulse and weight data

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rr2graph
[\-c config.yaml]
[\-\-info]
[\-\-version]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rr2graph
is a lightweight command-line tool for processing and visualizing
blood pressure, pulse and weight measurements from Excel files.
It generates monthly charts (box-swarm, scatter, histogram, violin)
and exports them as PNG, PDF and SVG.

The tool reads a YAML configuration file that specifies input data,
output directories and plot settings.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to the YAML configuration file. Defaults to \fIconfig.yaml\fR
in the current directory.

.TP
.BR \-\-info
Show environment, configuration and installation details.

.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show program version and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is written in YAML and contains:

.TP
.B input_file
Path to the Excel file containing measurement data.

.TP
.B output_dir
Directory where generated plots will be saved.

.TP
.B plots
List of plot types to generate (e.g. box, swarm, scatter, histogram, violin).

Example:

.nf
input_file: ~/OneDrive/rr_data.xlsx
output_dir: ~/OneDrive/rr_plots
plots:
  - box
  - swarm
  - scatter
.fi

.SH EXAMPLES
Generate plots using the default configuration:

.nf
rr2graph
.fi

Use a custom configuration file:

.nf
rr2graph -c config.yaml
.fi

or with configs more centralized at your HOME

.nf
rr2graph -c ~/configs/rr2graph.yaml
.fi

Show diagnostic information:

.nf
rr2graph --info
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.yaml
Default configuration file.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
General error (invalid config, missing input file, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
python(1), yaml(5)

